{"text": "PARK 500\nINTER-OFFICE CORRESPONDENCE\nCHESTER, VIRGINIA\n\nNovember 18, 1992\n\nTo: Distribution\nFrom: Faye E, Hunter\n\nSubject: RECORDS MANAGEMENT\n\nIn order for me to perform my duties competently as Records Coordinator for Maintenance\nand Lab Services I must know \"who\" the employees are in the two departments and \"what\"\npositions they hold, I need to know when new employees come into the department as well\nas employees leaving the department. If there is a change in the \"players\", I need to know\nthis information in order to do my job as Records Coordinator. Also, when employees leave\nthe department, whether they are transferring to another department at Park 500, a different\nlocation, or leaving the Company, I need to know the disposition of their records. Records\nshould not be disposed of until consulting with the Records Management Analyst for that\ndepartment. If another employee absorbs the records, I need to know this so the individual\u2019s\n\ninventory is updated.\n\nIn the past I have obtained the above such information through the \"grapevine\". I'm sure\nyou agree with me that this is not an efficient method of communication. Your assistance in\nproviding me with this information is appreciated and will help us to assure that our\ndepartments are in compliance with the Philip Morris USA Records Management Policies\nand Procedures.\n\n\u2018fh/a:001.rr\nDISTRIBUTION: _W. H. Bailey\nK. G, Braun\nT.\n\n2\n\nce: T. M. Ratliff\n\n82T90Ts0\u00a2",
